WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.897
(Music)

00:00:08.897 --> 00:00:10.106
I want you to publish this. 

00:00:10.106 --> 00:00:12.150
You're finally gonna let me
publish one of your poems?

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.443
But you can't print my name. 

00:00:13.443 --> 00:00:14.444
Why not?

00:00:14.444 --> 00:00:16.613
Because my father doesn't
approve of women publishing.

00:00:16.613 --> 00:00:20.700
(Music)

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.788
Hailee Steinfeld:
What's so incredible about
playing a person that existed lifetimes ago

00:00:24.788 --> 00:00:26.581
Hailee Steinfeld:
is her story and her voice is so

00:00:26.581 --> 00:00:29.125
relatable in what she faces
everyday as a young woman.

00:00:29.125 --> 00:00:33.505
I do not approve of a woman
seeking a literary reputation!

00:00:33.505 --> 00:00:36.007
Alena Smith:
Woman in a certain sense were
property.

00:00:36.007 --> 00:00:38.260
You will tend to your duties as
your mother does.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.428
Alena Smith:
And we're trying to find the

00:00:40.428 --> 00:00:44.391
uncanny residences between the
1850's and today.

00:00:44.391 --> 00:00:48.186
In this house what matters is
what your father wants.

00:00:49.771 --> 00:00:55.068
We're not doing a bio pic of
Emily Dickinson in any kinda
straight forward sense.

00:00:55.068 --> 00:00:59.030
Alena Smith:
We are doing our own poetic
interpretation of Emily Dickinson.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:02.868
Alena Smith:
To create a modern and feminist
retelling of her life.

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:06.079
Mrs. Dickinson:
You're gonna make a good house
wife one day Emily Dickinson.

00:01:06.079 --> 00:01:07.873
It's high time for you to get a
husband.

00:01:08.498 --> 00:01:12.377
Emily has this need for
intellectual stimulation

00:01:12.377 --> 00:01:15.797
Ella Hunt:
and to be seen as the equal of
men.

00:01:15.797 --> 00:01:16.756
Why won't you marry me?

00:01:16.756 --> 00:01:18.550
I'm not gonna marry anyone.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:19.759
Hailee Steinfeld:
She believe in herself.

00:01:19.759 --> 00:01:21.803
She was a practical woman who

00:01:21.803 --> 00:01:24.222
Hailee Steinfeld:
was completely aware of her
gifts.

00:01:24.222 --> 00:01:25.891
Why can't I go to the college?

00:01:25.891 --> 00:01:28.101
Look, an education prepares one
for a career.

00:01:28.101 --> 00:01:29.769
And a career of a woman is in
the home.

00:01:29.769 --> 00:01:31.271
Hailee Steinfeld:
Even though she was told that
her work

00:01:31.271 --> 00:01:32.606
will never see the light of
day.

00:01:32.606 --> 00:01:34.941
Hailee Steinfeld:
That never stopped her.

00:01:34.941 --> 00:01:35.942
Hailee Steinfeld:
She kept going. 

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:38.653
It's not up to my father to
decide my fate.

00:01:38.653 --> 00:01:40.071
And it's not up to you.

00:01:40.071 --> 00:01:43.241
Hailee Steinfeld:
Knowing that her way with words
have had an impact 

00:01:43.241 --> 00:01:44.910
on so many people around the
world

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.661
is incredibly inspirational.

00:01:46.661 --> 00:01:48.580
And it's been wonderful to bring
that to life. 

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:52.584
(Music)

